726:**Controls and the filtered tree (ALFS).** ALFS is the DC form of FG-SA, registered as `fj.frame.v2` (registry commit `4bc6690`; source key `alfs`, the archived spec `spec/archive/fgsa-protocol-183f2c40.tex`; proof file `ldp`, `fgsa-live-dc-port.md`). In ALFS the frame has two parts:
727:- the CONTROLS `(F, H, j, J, contest)`, with the derived root `Z` and band floor `lo` (`fg_contest`, `band_floor` and `get_fg_root`, `alfs` lines 910–926 and 944–951). ALFS reads them from the FULL store, as DC's live caches: `F = Σ.F`, `H = Σ.hmax`, `(j, J) = (Σ.h_j, Σ.J)`, and the contest over `Σ.T_F`. Task 7's `storeControls` is this form, and `storeControls_eq_fjControls` shows that it equals `fjControls Σ.F Σ.T_F` under the store invariant;
728:- the FILTERED TREE `filteredFrom c blocks` over an explicit block set: `get_filtered_block_tree_from(Σ, blocks)` (`alfs` lines 953–960), that is `viable_tree_from(Σ, blocks)` (lines 928–934) cut at the root, `{B ∈ blocks : F ⪯ B, Z ⪯ B, ∃ W ∈ blocks, B ⪯ W, h(W) ≥ lo}`. The HEAD walks it over DC's frozen voter tree (`voter_processed_block_tree` and `voter_filtered_block_tree`, lines 1144–1159; the HEAD duty call, lines 1220–1222) with the full-store controls; the proposal, the FG action and the finality head use the full tree `Σ.T_F` (`get_filtered_block_tree`, lines 961–965). The block sets, the walk start `live_root` (lines 1014–1026: the deepest live lease in the full filtered tree, else the FG root) and `get_head_in_tree` (lines 1028–1035) are AP data.
730:`fjControls F Vw` computes the controls from one block set (r148 `FJ_FRAME`, the R1 view form), and `fjFrame F Vw` is the special case that uses one set for both parts. Every lemma states which form it is about (Tasks 7, 12 and 13).
732:The FG module exports the FRAME only: the controls, `Z`, `lo`, the filtered tree (viability), and `frontier`/`lexMax`. `fjControls` and `fjFrame` take F as a PARAMETER (Global Constraints: never the current accepted F). The majority threshold, the current-slot rule, the GHOST score and the walk are AP (Goldfish/SA) fork-choice machinery (user decision 2026-09-28). They are NOT in this module. Head selection (`fgsa_head` in r148 §2) and eligibility are AP data. The `fj.frame.v1` pin is therefore partial: "frame only (Z, lo, D, viability); fgsa_head and eligibility are AP data, see ap.headReachesLo.v1".
