818:  The fallback `(0, genesis)`: if `F ≠ genesis` and no pair in the view extends F, then `J = genesis`, and `F ⪯ J` fails. In ALFS the controls come from the full store, which holds the block that finalized F (`StoreInv.Fcar`, Task 7), so the fallback is not used there. Task 7's `lexMax_of_candidate` (a helper) proves that the fallback is not used when the block set holds a block whose J extends F and `ViewRootInj` holds. Keep the fallback; do not change it to `(h_F, F)`, because the spec does not say so.
