872:**Where the controls come from (ALFS).** ALFS (`fj.frame.v2`; the archived spec `alfs`, `spec/archive/fgsa-protocol-183f2c40.tex`; proofs in `ldp`, `fgsa-live-dc-port.md`) is DC §7 with two changes: the SA base and the FJ rule on DC's live caches. The frame CONTROLS come from the FULL store, as DC's live caches: `F = Σ.F`, `H = Σ.hmax`, `(j, J) = (Σ.h_j, Σ.J)`, and the contest bit over `Σ.T_F` ("Contest from the full store": it uses the same store as `Σ.hmax` and `Σ.J`, so it does not mix a live cache with a frozen view, r148 §2). `storeControls st` is this object. It is the source of the controls for every duty: the HEAD applies it to DC's frozen voter tree, and the proposal, the FG action and the finality head apply it to the full tree `Σ.T_F`. So `storeControls_eq_fjControls` is the CENTRAL lemma of this task: under `StoreInv`, the live caches are exactly the controls that r148's `FJ_FRAME` computes from the full admitted tree. (The previous revision called this object `cacheFrame`, a "comparison object"; that wording followed the R1 spec, which ALFS removes.)
874:ALFS deletes the R1 view frames, the F basis and the J carrier. The facts that the F basis supplied to duty views now come from the full store: the block that finalized F is in `Σ.T_F` (`StoreInv.Fcar`), and the controls are read there. The block set of a duty (the frozen HEAD tree) enters only as the `blocks` argument of `filteredFrom`.
876:The pure view lemmas still take F and their premises as hypotheses (Global Constraints). Each lemma states its form: `fjControls` of a block set, `filteredFrom` with ANY block set, or the `fjFrame` special case.
