1102:  - FG admission: a store literal with `F = B1` and `T = TF = {genesis, B1}`, and a block `B1'` (slot 2, parent genesis, root `⟨3⟩`, three target rows at height 1 for genesis). `on_block` adds `B1'` to `T` only: `TF` and `h_max` do not change;
1103:  - the guards (alfs line 750): `on_block` of a block already in `T`, and of a block whose parent is not in `T`, returns the store unchanged.
1105:  - `storeInv_on_block`:
1106:    - If the guard of `on_block` returns (`B ∈ st.T` or `B.parent ∉ st.T`), the store does not change. Otherwise `B ∉ st.T` and `B.parent ∈ st.T`.
1108:    - `admits`: a new block with `F ⪯ B` enters `TF`. F only moves to a descendant (`update_finality_F_mono`), so `F' ⪯ X` implies `F ⪯ X`, and `X ∈ TF` by the old invariant.
1110:    - `Fmem`: F moves only to `σ.F ∈ acceptViable ⊆ TF`.
1113:    - `Fcar`: at an acceptance, `B ∈ TF` (it was just admitted) and `(derive B).F = σ.F`. Otherwise F does not change and `TF` grows. `derive` is a function of the block, so the carrier keeps its F.
