+- [ ] **Step 4: Write `scripts/check-fg-syntax.sh`** (Astra H06). It finds the `native_decide` token outside comments. The environment does not keep `example`s, so `CheckFGAxioms.lean` cannot see them. `sorry` and `admit` need no scan: `lake build --wfail` fails on them.
+
+```bash
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# Fails if a .lean file of the two FG libraries uses the token native_decide
+# outside a comment. Block comments /- … -/ and line comments -- are removed
+# first (Lean block comments nest; the FG files do not nest them).
+set -euo pipefail
+cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
+files=$(find AvailableChainSimplexFG AvailableChainKitFG AvailableChainSimplexFG.lean \
+  AvailableChainKitFG.lean -name '*.lean' 2>/dev/null || true)
+[ -n "$files" ] || { echo "NO FILES"; exit 2; }
+status=0
+for f in $files; do
+  if perl -0777 -pe 's{/-.*?-/}{}gs; s{--[^\n]*}{}g' "$f" |
+      grep -nE '(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_.])native_decide([^A-Za-z0-9_]|$)' >/dev/null; then
+    echo "native_decide in $f"; status=1
+  fi
+done
+exit $status
+```
+
+  Negative test (once, then remove it): add `example : 1 = 1 := by native_decide` to `Objects.lean`; the script must exit 1. A comment `-- native_decide` and a name such as `admits` must not make it fail.
